From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:03:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: keep a T8132 root port's DART gated until
 the port is up

On T8132 the built-in PCIe host's root ports (the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth radio's
and the SD card reader's) each clock the DART behind them. A deep sleep
stops those ports, and apple-s2r powers ANS's APCIe block up again before
any device resumes, but only this host sets a stopped port up again, in
its noirq resume. The DARTs resume before it (they are its iommu-map
suppliers) and, their power cut, restore their state at once: the first
read of a translation register goes to a port that is not clocked, and
the SoC raises an SError. A split sleep at depth 7 panics there (PMU
stage 0x37 with resume_trail, its DART time slot). A real sleep marks the
same ports down and would stop at the same read.

apple-dart already has the gate for this case
(apple_dart_set_host_resumes() and apple_dart_host_resume()), but nothing
set it. Set it at probe for the DART that each T8132 root port's secondary
bus maps to, and after the noirq restart resume the DART of every port
that is up. The DART of a port the sleep left down stays gated, as its
configuration space stays blocked.

Gate on any sleep that runs the firmware's path rather than only where
the DART lost its power: the ports stop before the block is lowered, so a
shallower split stops them with the power kept. The host ungates every
port that is up, stopped or not, so a port that kept running only gets
its TLBs dropped.

A host test runs the gate and the host's resume against a model in which
a DART's registers abort while its port is off, over the split depths, a
real sleep, suspend-to-idle and a runtime-active DART, and checks in the
T8132 device trees that every root port maps to its own enabled DART.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 MAINTAINERS                                  |   1 +
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c                   |   9 +-
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c          |  77 ++++
 tools/asahi/run-host-tests.py                |   3 +
 tools/asahi/t8132-apcie-dart-resume-tests.py | 365 +++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 452 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 tools/asahi/t8132-apcie-dart-resume-tests.py

diff --git a/MAINTAINERS b/MAINTAINERS
index 8cd7895af7..fd0b831fd3 100644
--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -2796,6 +2796,7 @@ F:	drivers/rtc/rtc-macsmc.c
 F:	drivers/soc/apple/*
 F:	tools/asahi/s2r-resume-trail-tests.py
 F:	tools/asahi/s2r-split-ans-tests.py
+F:	tools/asahi/t8132-apcie-dart-resume-tests.py
 F:	tools/asahi/m3-uapi-*
 F:	drivers/soc/apple/clpc.kunitconfig
